  "implementation": [
    "CoreSQL.insertRegisterRowsWith parameterizes the existing checked source loop over its monad and actual write emitter. The old pure API specializes the same implementation; source projection, predicates and LIMIT/OFFSET interpretation are shared.",
    "RegisterInput prepares real source/target metadata before execution starts. Its effectful emitter calls the common accepted-point executor and records only actual point states. Direct changes/total_changes finish once at the outer statement boundary.",
    "The source rows are the existing immutable table rows. The admitted producer is an external index-free plain-table scan without ordering, DISTINCT, compounds or captures; other plans retain their existing paths. No source/query values are fabricated.",
    "Empty AUTOINCREMENT completion uses the real sequence context and generated dependency checks remain preparation errors. The C VFS shim is unchanged."
  ],
  "evaluation_protocols": {
    "public_file_modes": "7156 stdout/exit/first-error and independent persisted catalog/row/integrity comparisons in rollback/WAL modes, including 56 new register input cases.",
    "same_connection": "122 actual Core state-carrying API comparisons against the pinned non-bailing shell, including fresh late source/predicate/constraint failures. This metric is separate from file comparisons.",
    "select_input_gaps": "12 deliberately failing/selectable regressions are reported separately: six pass and six remain real failures. They are never skipped or marked expected failures.",
    "named_features": "Eight failures in a separate 88-case named feature survey remain; neither survey defines global coverage."
  },
  "proof_scope": "Retained contracts and audits compile. The existing register-loop LIMIT-zero law now compiles over its shared monadic interpreter; a new audited component law keeps pending-state counter normalization independent of logical data. The maintained executable group checks late source/constraint error rowids, rollback data and yielded register values. No general SELECT coroutine equivalence theorem is claimed.",
  "limitations": [
    "Six of 12 maintained general SELECT-input regressions still fail; ordered/DISTINCT/compound and projected/flattened VALUES plans are next work.",
    "Wider error codes/phases, FAIL/IGNORE/ROLLBACK controls, triggered UPSERT, INSTEAD OF/temp triggers, writable CTEs, trigger-aware ALTER and deferred private-function declarations remain work.",
    "Eight of 88 named probes still fail: WITHOUT ROWID, composite primary keys and partial/expression indexes, both modes. These probes do not define global coverage.",
    "UTF-16 writes/setters, native-key/materialization limits, pending new physical allocations and earlier SQL/storage limitations remain. The finite process-kill samples do not establish every syscall/power-loss schedule."
  ],
